<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dümmer</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dümmer See</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dümmer is a shallow lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, near Diepholz, the second-largest lake in the state. Surrounded by moors and wet meadows and fed and drained by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunte">Hunte</a> river, it is an important reserve for water birds. Its shores are rich in remains of Stone Age settlement preserved in the peat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dummer.jpg" alt="Dümmer" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Specialplant at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duemmer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
